  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Kamati's Ledger",
    "overview": "Kadi Sasa should look like a wedding committee's well-kept ledger: calm, exact and trustworthy, with every figure in its column. The organiser counts guests and shillings, the gate agent admits a queue, and the guest checks that the invitation is real. None of them need decoration. They need the right number, the right name and the right next step, readable on a cheap Android phone in bright sun. Most of the system is plain tools: warm ivory paper, ink, and one deep emerald that marks where to act.\n\nCeremony has one home: the guest card and the printed card. There, the couple's names are set in a display serif, an East African-inspired ornament band runs in gold, and the cover takes the event's theme colour. Elsewhere the serif and ornament appear only as previews of that card. The console, the ops panel and the gate are crisp and precise. Edges are bordered and flat, figures are tabular, labels are short, and targets are large enough to hit without looking twice.\n\nThis system rejects three looks. It is not a generic SaaS dashboard: no purple gradients, glass cards or decorative charts. It is not a flashy wedding template: no glitter, script fonts, florals or ornamental motion. And it is not a government or bank form: nothing cold or bureaucratic that would intimidate an elder holding a printed card.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm ivory ground (`bg`) under white working surfaces, separated by linen borders rather than shadows.",
      "One action colour (deep emerald). Gold is decoration only and never carries text.",
      "System sans for everything operational. The display serif is reserved for names on cards.",
      "Tabular figures wherever money, counts or codes appear.",
      "Every status is shown with colour, an icon and a word together.",
      "The QR is always pure black on pure white, whatever the theme.",
      "Touch targets are 48 px or more, inputs are never below 16 px, and the layout works at 360 px first."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Ink of Action Rule",
        "body": "Emerald means \"act here or you are here\". Don't use it for decoration, headings or large background areas in the console. If everything is emerald, nothing is clickable.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Gold Never Speaks Rule",
        "body": "Gold is never used for text, icons with meaning, or status. It decorates only.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
